WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.240
Let's face it: It's always satisfying&nbsp;
to watch "Stranger Things" baddies get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:07.520
what's coming to 'em. As far&nbsp;
as Season 4 goes, it seems as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:11.120
if the death of one antagonist&nbsp;
was foreshadowed very early on.

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:16.720
After Vecna, Jason Carver could be considered the&nbsp;
next major "Stranger Things" Season 4 antagonist.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:20.960
As the captain of the Hawkins High School&nbsp;
basketball team, Jason is popular enough&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:26.080
to command most of his teammates on and off the&nbsp;
court, leading them on a witch hunt for Eddie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:30.480
whom he believes is responsible for his&nbsp;
girlfriend's death at the end of Episode 1.

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:33.200
Before this, however, he and&nbsp;
the team celebrate winning the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:37.520
championship game by drinking at Benny's&nbsp;
now-abandoned restaurant. The next morning,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:40.880
Jason describes being hungover&nbsp;
as like being split in two.

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:44.240
"First hangover feels like&nbsp;
you're gonna split in two."

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:49.440
In fact, this is exactly what happens to him after&nbsp;
Vecna shatters the boundary between this world&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:54.240
and the Upside Down, essentially cleaving&nbsp;
Jason right down the middle. In the end,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:57.840
he knows full well what being&nbsp;
split in two really feels like.

